.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-PROXY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-proxy
.Nd the web console's former single-port TLS proxy, kept to start by hand if nginx will not
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A browser trusts a certificate per host and port, so a console that sent
it to Grafana on one port and a terminal on another asked it to accept
the certificate again for each, and blocked the frames outright.
.Nm
listens on port 8443 with the machine's certificate and forwards by path
to services on loopback:
.Pa /grafana/
to Grafana on 3000,
.Pa /k9s/
to the k9s terminal on 7681, and everything else to the web console on
8444, WebSockets included.
.Pp
.Xr nginx 8
has done this since 1.0.6.
.Nm
and its unit remain as a way back: the unit is not enabled and nothing
starts it.
Stop nginx before starting it, since both want port 8443.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, serving nothing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt , Pa webui.key
The certificate, from
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 .
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/kldload-proxy.service
Its unit, which makes the certificate first.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
It serves until stopped; non-zero when it cannot bind the port or read
the certificate.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Falling back to it; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# systemctl stop nginx
# systemctl start kldload-proxy
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-session 8 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Paths the web console gained after 1.0.6 \(em
.Pa /s/
sessions and
.Pa /app/
tools \(em are routed only by nginx.
